    "created_at": "2016-10-17T23:58:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-17T23:58:18Z",
    "body": "> In my mind, the shortest path to simplicity and interop here is to converge on the Edge/Firefox behavior. That would mean updating the spec to say \"The start IDL attribute has a default value of 1.\" (Right now it says \"The start IDL attribute has the same default as its content attribute\", but that doesn't make any sense.)\n\nI think this is fine. I don't have preference on whether the default value should be 0 or 1. Picking the shortest path sounds good.\n",
